    <briefdescription>
<para>Allocate memory local to a NUMA node. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>When <computeroutput>libnuma</computeroutput> is available (guarded by <computeroutput>THEMIS_ENABLE_NUMA</computeroutput>) the allocation is placed on the specified node. Otherwise the request falls through to <computeroutput>std::aligned_alloc</computeroutput>.</para>
<para>Allocations are always aligned to at least 64 bytes (cache line). </para>
    </detaileddescription>
